# H4 (run 4 of 5): the AUDITS-OFF HANG SHAPES at eight seats on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1 (the W1 stack on the control's audits-off profile). Two changes bear on the hang, which is unexplained and sensitive to the trace shape: the in-trace sampler is gone (nosamp: the
# request-width warm is the only fix left, hang-safe 3 of 3 on its own) and about 20 ms of host time between traces is gone (the host-gap stage 1), on top of the drafter ops and the unit-major reduce-scatter in the traces. Five consecutive completions are required.
# The shapes: concurrent4_steady, concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix), steady_resend, replay_concurrent4 and replay_concurrent8, the exactness reference concurrent8_code_equal, then the split-block and drain shapes. Each run follows its own all-four reset.
# READ: every user at budget, c2_smoke_check clean, no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, the concurrent8_code_equal hashes equal in every run and equal to the control's (S0c). No stall watch on this profile: a stall waits for the job timeout and
# records nothing, which is itself the finding. Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule: one stall stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w1 eight-seat 262k stack window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,replay_concurrent8,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
